{
  "name": "@terpatin/lerpyderpy",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "https://github.com/HannulaTero/LerpyDerpy \r\nhttps://terohannula.itch.io/lerpyderpy \r\nThe asset handles making values approach with smooth motion, allowing bounciness and overshooting. \r\nIn this asset there is `Lerpy` and `LerpyDerpy`.\r\n`Lerpy` is the actual lerper construct, and `LerpDerpy` is collection of lerpers. The collection attaches new lerper to given field _(scope and key)_, so updating the collection automatically updates attached fields. `Lerpy` is not attached to field without `LerpyDerpy`, and can be used as stand-alone. \r\nAttaching fields to `LerpyDerpy` returns the `Lerpy`, which can be used to change the target point or its parameters. Updating `LerpyDerpy` updates the fields accordingly, \r\nbut you can also utilize `.PullTargets()` and `.PushTargets()` to change fields yourself, and these changes are assigned as new targets.",
  "files": [
    "com.terpatin.lerpyderpy-1.0.0.yymps"
  ],
  "keywords": [
    "lerp",
    "mix",
    "interpolate",
    "momentum"
  ],
  "author": "Terpatin",
